save last_topic = "nothing yet"

Welcome to the Bobbin Syntax Guide!
I'll teach you how to write dialogue scripts.
Your last topic was: {last_topic}
What would you like to learn about?

- Basic text lines
    set last_topic = "text lines"
    The simplest thing in Bobbin is plain text.
    Each line becomes one dialogue box.
    Like this! Three lines, three boxes.
    That's all there is to basic dialogue!

- Choices with the - symbol
    set last_topic = "choices"
    Choices start with a dash and a space.
    Everything indented under a choice happens when selected.
    Let me show you a nested example...
    Pick a color:
    - Red
        You chose red! Bold choice.
    - Blue
        Blue it is! A calming selection.
    Nested choices work the same way!

- The save keyword
    set last_topic = "save keyword"
    Use "save" to declare persistent variables.
    Example: save gold = 100
    These remember their value between conversations!
    I'm using save to remember your last topic.
    Talk to the Memory Keeper to see another example.

- The set keyword
    set last_topic = "set keyword"
    Use "set" to change a variable's value.
    Example: set mood = "happy"
    I just used set to update your last topic!
    Come back and you'll see it remembered.

- The extern keyword
    set last_topic = "extern keyword"
    Use "extern" to access game variables.
    Example: extern player_health
    The game passes these in via host_state.
    Talk to the Oracle to see this in action!

- Display variables with curly braces
    set last_topic = "variable display"
    Put variable names in curly braces to show their value.
    Your current topic is: {last_topic}
    This works with save, set, and extern variables!

Come back anytime to review. Happy writing!
